  "description": "Reid Tanami 2 Gravel eBike | Electric gravel bike\nBuilt for exploring further, the Tanami 2 combines a versatile gravel setup with smooth electric assistance to help you take on longer rides and challenging terrain.\nThe Reid Tanami 2 builds on the original Tanami, bringing upgraded components and an Ananda electric system to our eGravel range. Designed for mixed-surface riding and off-road exploration, it combines the versatility of a gravel bike with the added support of pedal assistance.\nThe 6061 alloy frame features an integrated 36V 352Wh battery and internal cable routing for a clean, streamlined design. A rigid 700c alloy fork with thru-axle provides responsive handling, while the integrated battery keeps the overall appearance neat and uncluttered.\nAn Ananda 250W rear hub motor delivers smooth electric assistance to support riders on hills and longer routes. The integrated display features Bluetooth connectivity through the Ananda app, allowing riders to access essential ride information. The 352Wh battery provides an approximate range of up to 30 miles (48km), depending on terrain and riding style.\nA Shimano CUES 10-speed drivetrain offers reliable shifting across varied terrain, paired with a wide-range cassette to help tackle changing gradients. Shimano hydraulic disc brakes provide controlled stopping power when riding on gravel paths and rougher trails.\nThe Tanami 2 is equipped with wide WTB gravel rims and 45mm WTB Riddler tyres. Both are tubeless-ready, giving riders the option to set up their wheels tubeless for their preferred gravel riding setup.\nCombining electric assistance, versatile gearing and gravel-ready components, the Tanami 2 is designed to help riders explore further and enjoy more of the routes less travelled.\nThe Tanami 2 eBike is ideal for:\n\nGravel riding and exploration, with a versatile setup for mixed surfaces and off-road routes\n\nTackling hills and longer rides, supported by a 250W Ananda rear hub motor and integrated 352Wh battery\n\nEveryday electric assistance, with a Bluetooth-connected display and app compatibility\n\nRiding on varied terrain, with Shimano CUES 10-speed gearing and a wide-range cassette\n\nControlled stopping power, with Shimano hydraulic disc brakes\n\nTubeless-ready gravel riding, with WTB rims and 45mm WTB Riddler tyres\n\nExploring further, with an approximate range of up to 30 miles (48km), depending on riding conditions\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
